 g\, Room 1.25\n\n Sign up\n\n About \n\n Speaker: Dr Miharu Hirano (Associ
 ate Professor\, Graduate School of Law\, Kobe University)\n Assessing the 
 safety of water for human health and the environment is not a purely scie
 ntific inquiry\; rather\, determining an acceptable level of risk is inex
 tricably linked to normative value judgments. How effectively internation
 al law guides States through such complex issues is frequently tested in
  novel contexts lacking clear precedent. Japan’s discharge of tritium-c
 ontaining ‘ALPS-treated water’ offers an interesting case study\, not
  only for the global attention it has attracted\, but also for the import
 ant legal questions it has raised. \n The Cambridge Centre for Environment
