SUMMARY:CIPIL Evening Seminar: 'Beyond Sync: Copyright\, Collective Managem
 ent and the Licensing of Music in Interactive Games'
LOCATION:Faculty of Law\, G24
URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/press/events/2026/11/cipil-evening-seminar-be
 yond-sync-copyright-collective-management-and-licensing-music-interactive
CATEGORIES:Law
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nTopics: Law\nDetails: https://www.law.cam.ac.uk
 /press/events/2026/11/cipil-evening-seminar-beyond-sync-copyright-collecti
 ve-management-and-licensing-music-interactive\nDate/time: \n\n Thursday 19
  November 2026 \n\n 5:30pm to 6:30pm\n\n Location: \n\n Faculty of Law\, G
 24\n\n About \n\n Speaker: Professor Sabine Jacques\, University of Liver
 pool\n Abstract: Music licensing for video games remains modelled on film
  and television synchronisation\, a framework premised on a fixed recordin
 g matched to a fixed sequence of images. Contemporary games increasingly d
 epart from that premise: scores adapt to player state\, generative systems
  produce a different rendition on each playthrough\, spatial audio makes t
 he player's movement part of the performance\, and persistent shared world
 s turn listening into a collective\, networked activity. This lecture exa
 mines the doctrinal and structural consequences of that shift. It consider
 s:how far adaptive and generative uses engage the rights of reproduction a
 nd adaptation\, and the author's moral right to object to derogatory treat
 ment\; whe
END:VEVENT
