  \n About In Memoriam Andreas von Hirsch (1934-2026) \n The Institute of C
 riminology is indebted to Andreas von Hirsch in many and profound ways. We
  will mention just three. First\, because he was a valued member of the In
 stitute for many years\; second because he was an extraordinarily generous
  benefactor\; and third because he was a towering intellectual figure in h
 is own right. He was a pioneering force in taking seriously the connection
 s between criminology and related fields – and both criminology and thos
 e other fields are much enriched by the interdisciplinary relationships hi
 s work contributed so d
