SUMMARY:CFL/Cambridge Socio-Legal Group Seminar: 'The evolution of parentho
 od in Brazil: from the single-parent stigma to multiple parenthood'
LOCATION:Faculty of Law\, G24
URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/events/cflcambridge-socio-legal-group-seminar
 -evolution-parenthood-brazil-single-parent-stigma
CATEGORIES:Law
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nTopics: Law\nDetails: https://www.law.cam.ac.uk
 /events/cflcambridge-socio-legal-group-seminar-evolution-parenthood-brazil
 -single-parent-stigma\nDate/time: \n\n Monday 25 January 2027 \n\n 1:00pm 
 to 2:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Faculty of Law\, G24\n\n About \n\n Speaker: 
 Professor João Costa-Neto (University of Brasília)\n Abstract: Brazilian
  family law has undergone a remarkable transformation: from a system built
  around marriage\, biological descent and exclusive parenthood to one incr
 easingly willing to recognise families as they are actually lived. This ta
 lk will trace that evolution\, focusing on the rise of socioaffective pare
 nthood and the idea that being a parent may result not only from biology\,
  but also from care\, responsibility and the social reality of family life
 . It then explores the most striking consequence of that shift: multiple p
 arenthood\, under which biological and socioaffective parents may coexist 
 with equal legal status. Drawing on constitutional change\, legal scholars
 hip and recent case law\, we will understand how Brazil mo
END:VEVENT
